```suggestion
#include "core/variant/array.h
#include "core/variant/dictionary.h"
```

You are using `typed_array.h` to access `dictionary.h` and `array.h` through `type_info.h` -> `variant.h`. Unless I am mistaken, these two are the only includes you need, not all the rest of the baggage that comes with.

```suggestion
#include "core/variant/dictionary.h"
#include "core/variant/typed_array.h"
```

In this case, you need the `typed_array.h` include, but should still explicitly include `dictionary.h` since you are using the `Dictionary` class.
